# CLIPFORGE — example environment variables (FRONTEND only).
# Copy to .env for local development. Never put real secrets in
# frontend files or commit a real .env file.
#
# Verified by full-codebase inventory (Phase 13, 2026-11-02):
# VITE_API_URL is the ONLY environment variable the frontend reads
# (src/services/api.ts:9 — import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL). Every other
# variable in this project belongs to the server — see
# server/.env.example and docs/ENVIRONMENT.md for the full list of
# 85 application variables.
#
# IMPORTANT: Vite inlines VITE_* values into the shipped JavaScript
# bundle at BUILD time. Anything placed here is public by design —
# never put an API key, token, or secret in a VITE_* variable.

# Backend base URL. By default the frontend calls "/api" same-origin
# (the Vite dev server proxies it to the backend on port 3001 — see
# server/.env.example for the server's own variables). Only set this
# when the API is hosted on a different origin. A production build
# that sets this must be rebuilt to change it.
# VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3001/api
#
# Free-tier integrations (ALL server-side — never VITE_*): stock
# B-roll unlocks with a free PEXELS_API_KEY (pexels.com/api) and real
# email delivery with a free SMTP account (Brevo free 300/day or
# Resend free tier) via SMTP_HOST/SMTP_PORT/SMTP_USER/SMTP_PASS/
# SMTP_FROM. Both are code-complete; see server/.env.example and
# docs/PROVIDERS.md ("Free-tier map") for the full picture.

# NODE_ENV is NOT read by the frontend source; Vite sets it itself
# (development for `vite`, production for `vite build`). Do not set
# it here expecting the app code to react — the server's NODE_ENV
# lives in server/.env (see server/.env.example).
